!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/validate-template-members.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/37/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/37/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  An enum template written in the positional form ([TSON-SCHEMA] §5.6): `!enum [a b M]` binds `members`,
  so `M` stands in a member position and an argument for it is a member, not a type name. `names<c>` is
  the enum with members a, b and c.
  """
{
  names => <M> !enum [a b M]

  holder => {
    n: names<c>
  }
}
